{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from an incredible trip to Japan, and my head is still spinning! It was a whirlwind of ancient temples, futuristic cities, and the most delicious food I've ever tasted.\n\nFirst stop: Kyoto. Wandering through Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates was truly breathtaking. The serene beauty of the Golden Pavilion (Kinkaku-ji) felt like stepping into a postcard. I even managed to catch a glimpse of a geisha gracefully making her way through Gion!\n\nThen it was off to Tokyo, a dazzling metropolis. Shibuya Crossing was an absolute must-see – a chaotic, yet strangely organized, human river. I explored the quirky shops of Harajuku, indulged in some incredible ramen, and spent an afternoon lost in the vibrant Akihabara electronics district.\n\nBeyond the iconic sights, it was the little things that really made the trip special. The impeccable politeness of the people, the meticulous attention to detail in everything from food presentation to garden design, and the overall sense of calm amidst the bustling cities. \n\nI tried my best to navigate with a phrasebook (and a lot of pointing!), and while there were definitely moments of confusion, it only added to the adventure. Japan is a country that truly captivates the senses. I can't wait to go back!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.14268067479133606}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.0709894448518753}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.20859424769878387}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -0.8985664248466492}, {"token": "▁back", "logprob": -0